===Etymology===
From {{inh|gl|roa-opt|assi}}, from {{inh|gl|LL.|ac sīc}}. Closely parallel to {{cog|rup|ashi}}, {{cog|pt|assim}}, {{cog|ro|așa}}, {{cog|es|así}}. Compare also {{cog|ca|així}}, {{cog|fr|ainsi}}, {{cog|it|così}}.

===Adverb===
{{gl-adv}}

# [[so]], [[thus]]

====Derived terms====
* {{l|gl|así como}}
* {{l|gl|así que}}

==Spanish==

===Pronunciation===
{{es-pr}}

===Etymology 1===
{{inh+|es|osp|assí}}, from {{inh|es|LL.|ac sīc}}. Closely parallel to {{cog|rup|ashi}}, {{cog|pt|assim}}, {{cog|ro|așa}}. Compare also {{cog|ca|així}}, {{cog|fr|ainsi}}, {{cog|it|così}}.

====Adverb====
{{es-adv}}

# like this; like that; as such; [[thus]]; [[so]]; [[thereby]]; [[this way]], [[that way]]
#: {{ux|es|¡'''Así''' se hace! Lo hiciste genial.|Way to go! You did great.|lit='''That's how''' it's done!}}
#: {{ux|es|[[así es la vida|'''Así''' es la vida]].|[[such is life|'''Such''' is life]].}}
#: {{ux|es|Si no paras de hablar '''así''', vas a hacerme llorar.|If you don't stop talking '''like that''', you're going to make me cry.}}
{{synonyms|es|talmente}}
# {{lb|es|followed by a subjunctive clause}} {{n-g|used to express wishes of misfortune against someone, or to cast a spell}}
#: {{ux|es|¡'''Así''' reciba un dolor de cabeza!|'''I hope''' he gets a headache!}}
#: {{ux|es|'''Así''' hubiera sobrevivido.|'''I hope''' he survived.}}

